※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4585

※ The lifted type is what the answer is and not what is pointed at, so the words
※ on the definition and the words in the brackets are the same words.  What is
※ at an address is one value, reached through a reference.

@[startup, impure]
fn main() → u6:
    let a: &mut u32 = ⎕at(8u64, ⌜u32⌝)
    if a⌖ = 0u32: 0u6 else: 1u6
